# Excel workbooks — the legacy screener / migration source contains
# real RFP data and must not enter the repo. EXCEL_SOURCE_PATH in
# .env points each deployment at its own workbook location (OneDrive /
# SharePoint /
# whatever) so the path stays deployment-local.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
# ...except the public, example-only donor-intel template (NO real intel —
# 3 public-knowledge donors + the field spec). This is the one workbook meant
# to be published so forkers can populate their own intel. See
# docs/DONOR_INTEL_MIGRATION.md.
!docs/donor_intel_template.xlsx

# Local debug / scratch outputs
*.log
.cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Playwright browser binaries (heavy, downloaded by `playwright install`)
.playwright/
playwright/.local-browsers/

# Local curl/debug dumps
page.html

# Scratch web-page dumps (debugging extraction)
cg_*.html

# Local team roster for scripts/seed_team_users.py — real names/emails, never committed
data/team_roster.local.json

# Per-tenant uploaded Excel workbooks (tenant data, never committed)
.workbooks/

# Backups written before a destructive purge — every column of the rows that were
# deleted, which is live tenant data in a folder that is NOT otherwise ignored (only
# data/team_roster.local.json was, and four fixtures under data/verify are tracked).
# Three were sitting untracked during a 50-commit push: one `git add -A` from reaching
# GitHub with a tenant's own opportunities, funders and award values in them.
#
# They are kept, not deleted — a purge is only reversible while its backup exists — and
# the pattern is deliberately `purged_*` rather than the two filenames, because the next
# purge will write the next one and nobody will remember to add it.
data/purged_*

# Local secrets crib sheet - real API keys in plaintext, never committed.
# The authoritative values live in the deployment's own secrets store.
docs/secrets_database

# Pyodide scoring trial: generated copies of repo code and live rows
web/scripts/spike/fixture/

# Generated at build: the Python bundle and the manual copied from assets/help
web/public/py/
web/public/help/
web/src/generated/py-bundle-hash.ts
web/.parity/
